[size=4][color=#00ffff]OVERVIEW[/color][/size]
[b]Perfectly Valid Wards[/b] is an SKSE plugin that overhauls Skyrim's ward spells, making them behave like real magical shields.
Wards now block melee attacks, arrows, shouts, diseases, and cloak effects. They can also reflect projectile spells back at attackers. The mod includes a ward power HUD meter, configurable attacker feedback, Restoration XP for blocking, and extensive tweaking options.


[size=4][color=#00ffff]WHY ANOTHER WARD MOD?[/color][/size]
There have been other attempts to enhance ward spells, but most face key limitations:
[list]
[*][b]Consistency[/b]: Some mods only affect the player. [b]Perfectly Valid Wards[/b] applies to [b]both the player and NPCs[/b].[/*]
[*][b]Feedback[/b]: Hurt sounds or wrong impact effects still play. [b]Perfectly Valid Wards[/b] handles that.[/*]
[*][b]Compatibility[/b]: Ward changes are applied at runtime without overriding ward records in a plugin, avoiding ESP-level conflicts with other mods that edit wards.[/*]
[/list]


[size=4][color=#00ffff]FEATURES[/color][/size]

[b][color=#88ccff]Physical Blocking[/color][/b]
[list]
[*][b]Melee & Arrow Blocking[/b]: Separate toggles control melee attacks (including unarmed attacks and bashes) and arrows/crossbow bolts. Both are enabled by default and use a configurable blocking angle.[/*]
[*][b]Ward Power Cost[/b]: Physical damage drains Ward Power using a formula based on weapon damage and attacker skills.[/*]
[*][b]Attacker Feedback[/b]: Blocked power attacks can cause recoil. Blocked normal attacks can stagger the attacker. Both are configurable.[/*]
[*][b]Restoration XP[/b]: Gain Restoration experience based on damage blocked (not Block or Armor XP).[/*]
[*][b]No Stamina Cost[/b]: Ward blocking doesn't cost stamina.[/*]
[/list]


[b][color=#88ccff]Magic - Shouts[/color][/b]
[list]
[*][b]Shout Modes[/b]: Four modes control how wards interact with shouts:
[list]
[*][b]Vanilla[/b]: Wards absorb shouts completely (default game behavior).[/*]
[*][b]Break Only[/b]: Shouts damage/break the ward but don't affect the defender.[/*]
[*][b]Break + Stagger[/b]: Ward breaks and defender staggers.[/*]
[*][b]Break + Pass Through[/b]: Ward breaks and the shout hits the defender.[/*]
[/list]
[/*]
[*][b]Configurable Damage[/b]: Choose between instant ward break or fixed damage.[/*]
[*][b]Player Immunity[/b]: Option to exempt the player from shout mechanics.[/*]
[*][b]Automatic Detection[/b]: Offensive shouts are identified automatically based on effects, damage keywords, and delivery type.[/*]
[*][b]Shout Exclusions[/b]: Exclude specific shouts from ward mechanics.[/*]
[/list]


[b][color=#88ccff]Magic - Spell Reflection[/color][/b]
[list]
[*][b]Reflect Projectile Spells[/b]: Incoming spell projectiles bounce back toward the attacker.[/*]
[*][b]Auto-Aim or Forward[/b]: Reflected spells can target the attacker or fire straight ahead.[/*]
[*][b]Blame Control[/b]: Choose whether the original attacker or defender is blamed for reflected damage.[/*]
[*][b]Reflect on Break[/b]: Option to reflect even the spell that breaks the ward.[/*]
[*][b]Automatic Detection[/b]: Reflectable spells are identified automatically.[/*]
[*][b]Spell Exclusions[/b]: Exclude specific spells from reflection.[/*]
[/list]


[b][color=#88ccff]Magic - Effects[/color][/b]
[list]
[*][b]Disease Blocking[/b]: Wards can block disease transmission when facing the source.[/*]
[*][b]Cloak Blocking[/b]: Wards can block hostile cloak spell damage ticks.[/*]
[*][b]Cloak Damage[/b]: Blocked cloak ticks can optionally drain ward power.[/*]
[/list]


[b][color=#88ccff]Ward Tweaks[/color][/b]
[list]
[*][b]Instant Cast[/b]: Skip the casting delay before a ward activates. Enable this together with Instant Charge for quick blocking.[/*]
[*][b]Instant Charge[/b]: Wards charge to full power instantly.[/*]
[*][b]Charge Rate[/b]: Multiplier for ward charging speed.[/*]
[*][b]Magnitude[/b]: Multiplier for ward strength (max ward power).[/*]
[*][b]Cost[/b]: Multiplier for ward magicka cost.[/*]
[*][b]Player Team Only[/b]: Option to restrict tweaks to player and followers.[/*]
[/list]


[b][color=#88ccff]HUD & Perk Gates[/color][/b]
[list]
[*][b]Ward Meter[/b]: Displays current ward power on the HUD charge meter while casting.[/*]
[*][b]Perk Requirements[/b]: Each feature can require specific perks to unlock.[/*]
[*][b]Item Exclusions[/b]: Specific ward items (like Spellbreaker) can be configured to disable certain features.[/*]
[/list]


[size=4][color=#00ffff]COMPATIBILITY[/color][/size]
[list]
[*]Works on all major game versions (SE/AE/VR)[/*]
[*]Other mods that alter ward behavior or replace the same engine functions can conflict.[/*]
[*]The plugin is ESL-flagged. It adds new records and edits the vanilla hit dialogue to suppress pain grunts when blocking with a ward.[/*]
[*]I will do my best to fix compatibility with combat mods but please be advised that I do not use complex combat mods.[/*]
[*]Tested with Deadly Combat - works fine.[/*]
[*]Tested with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/62061]Andrealletius' Additional Spells[/url] - really nice vanilla+ spell pack, try it out[/*]
[*]Should work with extra mod added ward spells - please report if you try.[/*]
[*]The Scrambled Bugs [code]accumulatingMagnitude[/code] patch is detected and handled automatically.[/*]
[/list]


[size=4][color=#00ffff]CONFIGURATION[/color][/size]
You can edit the INI directly:

[quote]Data\MCM\Settings\PerfectlyValidWards.ini[/quote]

Or use the optional MCM addon to change the common settings in-game.

The MCM includes:
[list]
[*][b]General[/b] - Ward meter, perk gate options, debug logging[/*]
[*][b]Tweaks[/b] - Charge speed, magnitude, cost multipliers[/*]
[*][b]Physical[/b] - Melee/arrow blocking, stagger, XP scaling[/*]
[*][b]Shouts[/b] - Shout mode, damage, pass-through behavior[/*]
[*][b]Effects[/b] - Disease and cloak blocking[/*]
[*][b]Reflection[/b] - Spell reflection options[/*]
[/list]

The INI also includes options for perk requirements, extra disease/cloak spells, and exclusions. Use local FormIDs without the load-order prefix, in [code]0x1234~Plugin.esp[/code] format, separated by commas. See [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/articles/6629]FormIDs and You[/url] for examples. Restart the game after changing these settings.


[size=4][color=#00ffff]UPDATING TO 3.0.0[/color][/size]
Your existing [code]Data\MCM\Settings\PerfectlyValidWards.ini[/code] is still used. [b]Before launching the game after updating[/b], convert any perk, spell or exclusion lists from [code]Plugin.esp|0x1234[/code] to [code]0x1234~Plugin.esp[/code]. Entries left in the old format will be removed. Other settings carry over.

Alternatively, delete that INI to reset your settings. The mod generates a new one on the next launch.

Settings from the old [code]Data\SKSE\Plugins\PerfectlyValidWards.ini[/code] are no longer imported.


